---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

// TODO before publishing: confirm the legal entity name, governing law / venue and
// the contact address below with counsel. GOVERNING_LAW is a placeholder.
const ENTITY = 'venOS';
const CONTACT = 'hello@venos.app';
const GOVERNING_LAW = 'the State of Utah, United States';
const UPDATED = 'September 1, 2026';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Use — venOS"
  description="The terms that govern your use of venOS."
  heading="Terms of Use"
  updated={UPDATED}
>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of the venOS website and application. By creating an
    account or using the service, you agree to them. If you are agreeing on behalf of a
    business, you confirm you have authority to bind that business.
  </p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    venOS helps vendors track the profitability of events. It aggregates figures you enter
    together with data retrieved from systems you connect, such as your point-of-sale, and
    presents calculated results including revenue, cost of goods, labor, expenses, profit
    and sales-tax figures.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>venOS is not a substitute for professional advice.</strong> The figures the
    service produces — including profit, cost and any tax-related amounts or estimates —
    are calculated from the data available to it and are provided for your information
    only. They are not tax, accounting, legal or financial advice, and your actual
    liability depends on your full financial picture. Always confirm with a qualified
    accountant or tax professional before relying on any figure for filing, remittance or
    other decisions.
  </div>

  <h2>Beta service</h2>
  <p>
    venOS is offered during a beta period. Features may change, break or be removed, and
    the service may be unavailable at times. We do not guarantee that any calculation,
    integration or figure will be complete or accurate during the beta, and you should
    verify results independently before relying on them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 18 and provide accurate registration information.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for keeping your credentials secure and for activity under your account.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for the members you invite to your company and for their access.</li>
    <li>Tell us promptly at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> if you suspect unauthorized use.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the service unlawfully, or to store or transmit unlawful content.</li>
    <li>Attempt to access accounts, data or systems that are not yours.</li>
    <li>Probe, scan or test the security of the service, or interfere with its operation.</li>
    <li>Reverse engineer, scrape or copy the service except as permitted by law.</li>
    <li>Resell or provide the service to third parties without our written agreement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    You keep ownership of the data you enter and the data retrieved from systems you
    connect. You grant us the license needed to host, process and display that data in
    order to operate the service for you. We handle it as described in our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for having the right to provide the data you submit, including any
    information about your staff, such as names, hours and wage rates.
  </p>

  <h2>Connected services</h2>
  <p>
    When you connect a third-party service such as Square, you authorize us to access it
    on your behalf. Your use of that service remains governed by its own terms, and we are
    not responsible for its availability, accuracy or actions. If a provider changes or
    withdraws its API, features that depend on it may stop working.
  </p>

  <h2>Fees</h2>
  <p>
    Paid plans are billed in advance through Stripe on a recurring basis until cancelled.
    You authorize us to charge your payment method for the applicable fees. Fees are
    non-refundable except where required by law. We may change pricing on notice, effective
    at your next billing period. Free and beta access may be modified or ended at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancellation and termination</h2>
  <p>
    You may cancel at any time from your account settings; access continues to the end of
    the paid period. We may suspend or terminate an account that violates these terms or
    creates risk for the service or other users. On termination, your right to use the
    service ends and we will delete or return your data as described in the Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The service, including its software, design and content, belongs to {ENTITY} and its
    licensors. These terms grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to
    use the service, and nothing more.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind,
    express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and
    non-infringement. We do not warrant that the service will be uninterrupted, error-free,
    or that any figure it produces will be accurate or complete.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, {ENTITY} will not be liable for indirect,
    incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue,
    data or goodwill, arising from your use of the service — including reliance on any
    figure it produces. Our total liability for any claim relating to the service is
    limited to the greater of the amounts you paid us in the twelve months before the claim
    or one hundred US dollars.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations, so parts of this section may not
    apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Indemnity</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to indemnify {ENTITY} against claims arising from your data, your use of the
    service, or your violation of these terms or of applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of {GOVERNING_LAW}, without regard to conflict of
    law rules. Disputes will be brought in the courts located there, and you consent to
    that jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms as the service changes. We will update the date at the top,
    and for material changes we will give notice through the application or by email.
    Continuing to use the service after a change means you accept the revised terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
